cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use orca_auto in research or published work, please cite the software repository or the release you used."
title: "orca_auto: queue-first ORCA workflow automation for Linux and WSL"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sohn
    given-names: Dae Hyup
repository-code: "https://github.com/dhsohn/orca_auto"
url: "https://github.com/dhsohn/orca_auto"
license: MIT
version: "3.0.4"
date-released: "2026-08-27"
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - ORCA
  - density functional theory
  - transition states
  - workflow automation
  - research software
abstract: >-
  orca_auto is a queue-first runtime and observability layer for ORCA-centered
  computational chemistry workflows on Linux and WSL. It submits work durably,
  runs jobs under supervised workers, and records per-job state and reports,
  keeping ORCA input files as the chemistry-facing contract.
